\ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
\ src/full_node.fam — full node entry point.
\
\ The overall node program.  Today it brings up the BIN0/UDP chunk server module
\ (a running node seeds its own binary to peers, replacing tools/server.py); future
\ node behaviour (consensus, ledger, prover) hangs off this same entry.
\
\ Build order: lib/stdlib.fam  src/node_serve.fam  src/full_node.fam  (this file
\ last, so the module's words are defined).  We capture tabernacle's handoff args
\ (a2 = bind port, a3 = debug flag, a4 = img_base) at top level — before any
\ : word call can clobber a0-a4 — then hand them to the server module.
\ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

\ Relocate the ENTIRE fam runtime above the loaded image, then serve it in place.
\ init (stdlib) normally puts gp = img_base + code_size, then lays the RID stack
\ (pushed by every :word call), the variable region, the heap and the data stack
\ starting there -- right past the code, INSIDE the appended bible -- so they would
\ corrupt served chunks.  Set gp to the END of the image (img_base + img_size) and
\ re-run init so all of that lands ABOVE the image; the image then stays pristine
\ and we point the TX descriptors straight at it (no snapshot copy).
\ This MUST run before any :word call (the first RID push).
8322C7FD ,   \ lw  t0, -36(a4)   ( t0 = img_size, the bin_size config at img_base-36 )
B3015700 ,   \ add gp, a4, t0    ( gp = img_base + img_size = first byte past the image )
init         \ relay RID stack / vars / heap / data stack ABOVE the image

_a1 _a2 _a3 _a4 runsrv
